{"id":"59d623a1692279f1","group":"17","path":"17/17-df-model-completeness.md","title":"Model Completeness","display":"df-model-completeness — Model Completeness","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Model Theory (Chang & Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)","book_abbrev":"17","label":"17-df-model-completeness","aliases":["17-df-model-completeness"],"display":"df-model-completeness — Model Completeness","depends_on":["[[17-df-model]]","[[17-df-elementary-substructure]]"],"label_origin":"local-catalog","source_verification":"definition compared in supplied OCR; local vacuous extension to inconsistent theories","source_section":"3.5","source_result":"Model-completeness definition","source_pages_print":[186],"source_pages_djvu":[202],"legacy_label":"17-df-3.4.1","local_revision":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Model Theory (Chang &amp; Keisler, 3rd ed. 1990)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"17"},{"key":"label","html":"17-df-model-completeness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>17-df-model-completeness</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-model-completeness — Model Completeness"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"71ede582cb78a069\" href=\"?note=71ede582cb78a069\" title=\"17-df-elementary-substructure\">17-df-elementary-substructure</a></span></div>"},{"key":"label_origin","html":"local-catalog"},{"key":"source_verification","html":"definition compared in supplied OCR; local vacuous extension to inconsistent theories"},{"key":"source_section","html":"3.5"},{"key":"source_result","html":"Model-completeness definition"},{"key":"source_pages_print","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>186</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pages_djvu","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>202</span></div>"},{"key":"legacy_label","html":"17-df-3.4.1"},{"key":"local_revision","html":"content audit of supplied 17(1).zip; inherited source_verification and bibliographic fields not independently reverified"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\">\\(L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span>。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> (theory with model class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"53255a372e5c1ee8\" href=\"?note=53255a372e5c1ee8\" title=\"17-df-model\">17-df-model</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\subseteq_L,\\preceq_L\">\\(\\subseteq_L,\\preceq_L\\)</span> (substructure and elementary-substructure relations, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"71ede582cb78a069\" href=\"?note=71ede582cb78a069\" title=\"17-df-elementary-substructure\">17-df-elementary-substructure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L\">\\(\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L(T)\n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\n\\forall\\mathfrak{A},\\mathfrak{B}\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\mathfrak{A}\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak{B}\n\\to\n\\mathfrak{A}\\preceq_L\\mathfrak{B}\n\\bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L(T)\n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\n\\forall\\mathfrak{A},\\mathfrak{B}\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\mathfrak{A}\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak{B}\n\\to\n\\mathfrak{A}\\preceq_L\\mathfrak{B}\n\\bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>Carrier inclusion alone is insufficient: the smaller model must be an\n<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span>-substructure of the larger one before elementary inclusion can be required.</p>\n<p>原书 §3.5 印刷 p.186（DjVu202）先要求理论一致，再定义模型完全性。本地保留已有的空真扩展：当 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)=\\varnothing\">\\(\\operatorname{Mod}(T)=\\varnothing\\)</span> 时，形式谓词仍为真。因此它在一致理论上与原书定义对应，不能将原书的一致性约定默默用于本地全部调用。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-model]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"71ede582cb78a069","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[17-df-elementary-substructure]]","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-model","status":"resolved","id":"53255a372e5c1ee8","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$T$ (theory with model class $\\operatorname{Mod}(T)$, see [[17-df-model]])","embed":false},{"target":"17-df-elementary-substructure","status":"resolved","id":"71ede582cb78a069","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\subseteq_L,\\preceq_L$ (substructure and elementary-substructure relations, see [[17-df-elementary-substructure]])","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"L\\in\\mathrm{FirstOrderLanguages}","display":false},{"tex":"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\subseteq_L,\\preceq_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L(T)\n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\n\\forall\\mathfrak{A},\\mathfrak{B}\\in\\operatorname{Mod}(T)\\;\n\\bigl(\n\\mathfrak{A}\\subseteq_L\\mathfrak{B}\n\\to\n\\mathfrak{A}\\preceq_L\\mathfrak{B}\n\\bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"L","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{Mod}(T)=\\varnothing","display":false}],"bytes":1794,"backlinks":[{"id":"f89b3dbb5152ec03","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":3,"excerpt":"$L$ 固定，$T,T^*\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L$。\n$\\operatorname{Cotheory}_L$ 见 [[17-df-universal-consequences]]，$\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L$ 见 [[17-df-model-completeness]]。\n以下定义 $\\operatorname{ModelCompanion}_L(T^*,T)$；第一参数为候选伴随理论，第二参数为原理论。"},{"id":"31695c838dded93c","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"一致性约定：原书印刷 p.186（DjVu 202）的模型完全性定义限于一致理论；本条沿用 [[17-df-model-completeness]] 的本地谓词，保留不一致时的空真延拓。故来源对应在一致理论上按原书理解；不一致边界由模型类为空另行核对，不把该延拓冒称原书定义。"},{"id":"256a095d7318cb9c","anchor":"ref-9","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"一致性约定：原书印刷 p.186（DjVu 202）的模型完全性定义限于一致理论；本条沿用 [[17-df-model-completeness]] 的本地谓词，保留不一致时的空真延拓。故来源对应在一致理论上按原书理解；不一致边界由模型类为空另行核对，不把该延拓冒称原书定义。"},{"id":"67c0bbaaadf7a9b6","anchor":"ref-5","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L$ (model-completeness predicate, see [[17-df-model-completeness]])"},{"id":"378c046219546f74","anchor":"ref-8","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L$ (model-completeness predicate, see [[17-df-model-completeness]])"},{"id":"903e38bc688a0a59","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{ModelComplete}_L$ (model-completeness predicate, see [[17-df-model-completeness]])"},{"id":"d868412e4c7fb403","an